# Asset structure (Disk Golf)

When creating or moving **any file under `Assets/`**, follow `Assets/README.md` and `ProjectArtPaths.cs`.

## Quick placement

| Asset type | Location |
|------------|----------|
| Textures/sprites | `Assets/Art/<domain>/<feature>/` as `TEX_*.png` |
| Materials | Same folder as textures: `MAT_*.mat` |
| Prefabs | `Assets/Prefabs/Gameplay/` or `Assets/Prefabs/Course/` |
| ScriptableObjects | `Assets/Data/<category>/` |
| C# scripts | `Assets/Scripts/<domain>/` |
| Editor scripts | `Assets/Editor/` |
| Scenes (prototype) | `Assets/Scenes/Prototype/` |
| Third-party | `Assets/ThirdParty/` |
| UI mockups | `Assets/Art/UI/Reference/` |

## Never do

- Create top-level `Materials/`, `Textures/`, or dump PNGs into `Resources/`
- Hardcode asset paths — add constants to `ProjectArtPaths.cs`
- Add `Resources.Load` without updating `GameplayArtCatalog` + **Refresh Gameplay Art Catalog**

## Feature co-location examples

```
Art/Environment/Course/Fairway/TEX_Fairway_Albedo.png
Art/Environment/Course/Fairway/MAT_Fairway.mat
Art/Environment/Foliage/Source/FoliageSheet.png
Art/Environment/Foliage/Sprites/GrassLight_A.png
Art/Characters/Player/Thrower.png
```

## After creating runtime-loaded art

1. Add path to `ProjectArtPaths.cs` if new root
2. Wire into `GameplayArtCatalogBuilder.cs` if loaded at runtime
3. Document in `Assets/README.md` if introducing a new category
